  "   ```",
  "",
  "   The channel reply carries the note of what was done. The manager DM is for questions and escalation and a one-line note of what was done; it never carries a draft reply that belongs in the channel.",
  "7. If `<originating-surface>` has no connected surface in the connected-surfaces list, emit no actions and record that in `notes`.",
  "",
  "## Verification",
  "",
  "Read back and report:",
  "- The comment: the runbook's `<audit-expectation>` — for example the audit comment visible on `<record-id>`, or the comment identifier returned by `save_comment`.",
  "- The state: the ticket's state as the surface now reports it, matching the state sent in step 5 (or unchanged, for a partial result).",
  "- The thread note, when step 6 ran: the message posted in `<reply-thread>`.",
  "",
  "## Actions emitted",
  "",
  "Every run emits a typed `actions[]` array; prose with no actions is a broken run. Typical output for a complete result on the kanban surface:",
  "",
  "```json",
  "[",
  "  {\"tool\": \"mcp.call\", \"args\": {\"surface\": \"<originating-surface>\", \"tool\": \"save_comment\", \"toolArgsJson\": \"{\\\"issueId\\\": \\\"<record-id>\\\", \\\"body\\\": \\\"...\\\"}\"}},",
  "  {\"tool\": \"mcp.call\", \"args\": {\"surface\": \"<originating-surface>\", \"tool\": \"save_issue\", \"toolArgsJson\": \"{\\\"id\\\": \\\"<record-id>\\\", \\\"state\\\": \\\"<workflow state>\\\"}\"}}",
